Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Kubi reaches a gate with two exits zero and one In\Nour example the qubit was prepared
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.65,0:00:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,with equal chances When we measure in this basis we\Nobtain a single result We do not
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.93,0:00:16.28,Default,,0,0,0,,receive a list of every possibility Imagine one hundred\Nexperiments In each one we
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.29,0:00:20.74,Default,,0,0,0,,prepare the same state again and then measure it We may\Nobtain approximately fifty zeros
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.75,0:00:25.16,Default,,0,0,0,,and fifty ones but the exact numbers vary Repeating the\Npreparation is essential
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.85,0:00:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Measuring the same qubit again immediately after the\Nfirst measurement without an
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.34,0:00:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,additional transformation is not equivalent to\Nperforming a new independent experiment